  "preview": "Three siblings share $48 in a 1:2:3 ratio. How much does each receive? Then: what changes if the ratio shifts?",
  "body": {
    "goal": "Use ratio reasoning to partition a quantity into unequal shares, and reason about what changes when the ratio changes.",
    "studentPrompt": "Three siblings — Asha, Bina, and Cole — find $48 their grandma left for them. They agree to split it in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3 (Asha gets 1 share, Bina gets 2, Cole gets 3).\n\n1. How much does each sibling get?\n2. The next week, grandma leaves $84 to be split the same way. Without redoing all the work, how much does each sibling get?\n3. Now the siblings find $48 again, but they decide to split it in a 2 : 3 : 5 ratio instead. How much does each get now?\n4. Can you write a general rule for splitting an amount $T in the ratio a : b : c?",
    "image": {
      "alt": "Three siblings — Asha, Bina, and Cole — standing together near an envelope of money labeled $48.",
      "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 480 220\" font-family=\"system-ui, sans-serif\"><g stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"70\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"135\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"118\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"118\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"78\" y2=\"170\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"102\" y2=\"170\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"60\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"130\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"112\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"112\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"187\" y2=\"170\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"213\" y2=\"170\"/><circle cx=\"310\" cy=\"55\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#fff\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"128\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"289\" y2=\"110\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"331\" y2=\"110\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"296\" y2=\"170\"/><line x1=\"310\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"324\" y2=\"170\"/></g><g stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"#fff\"><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"68\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#333\"/><circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"68\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#333\"/><circle cx=\"196\" cy=\"58\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#333\"/><circle cx=\"204\" cy=\"58\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#333\"/><circle cx=\"306\" cy=\"53\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#333\"/><circle cx=\"314\" cy=\"53\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#333\"/></g><g stroke=\"#333\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M84 75 Q90 79 96 75\"/><path d=\"M194 65 Q200 69 206 65\"/><path d=\"M304 60 Q310 64 316 60\"/></g><g><rect x=\"370\" y=\"110\" width=\"90\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#d4efd4\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M370 110 L415 142 L460 110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"415\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1b5e20\">$48</text></g><g stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M108 118 Q200 100 365 130\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/><path d=\"M220 110 Q290 105 370 128\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/><path d=\"M325 108 Q345 110 368 124\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/></g><g fill=\"#333\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"90\" y=\"190\">Asha</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"190\">Bina</text><text x=\"310\" y=\"190\">Cole</text></g><g fill=\"#555\" font-size=\"12\" font-style=\"italic\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"415\" y=\"100\">Grandma's gift</text></g></svg>"
    },
    "launch": "Tell the story. Don't draw anything. Don't write anything. Just ask: 'How would you split $48 in a 1 to 2 to 3 ratio?' Hand out markers. Send them to the whiteboards.",
    "materials": [
      "Vertical whiteboards",
      "Markers"
    ],
    "concepts": [
      "ratios",
      "proportional-reasoning",
      "unit-rate",
      "scaling",
      "fair-share"
    ],
    "taskType": "investigation",
    "btcFit": "Strong BTC fit. Story-anchored, low floor (drawing 6 boxes works), high ceiling (the general rule with variables is grade 7+ algebra). Works well in groups of 3.",
    "anticipatedApproaches": "- Draw 6 boxes (1 + 2 + 3 = 6 parts) and divide $48 by 6. Each part is $8.\n- Use a ratio table.\n- Set up an equation: x + 2x + 3x = 48.\n- For Q3 (ratio 2:3:5 = 10 parts), some students will not realize the total parts changed and miscompute.",
    "commonMisconceptions": "- Confusing the RATIO (parts) with the FRACTION of the total. 1:2:3 is NOT '1/3, 2/3, 3/3' — it's 1/6, 2/6, 3/6.\n- Forgetting that the number of total parts changes when the ratio changes.\n- Treating each share as 'one slice' (= $48 / 3 = $16) instead of using the ratio.",
    "discussionQuestions": "- How do you know the youngest sibling gets the least? Where does that show up in your work?\n- What stays the same between problems 1 and 2? What changes?\n- If we change the ratio from 1:2:3 to 2:3:5, why does the share size change even though the total is the same?\n- Whose method do you find clearest? Why?",
    "extensions": "- The siblings agree to redistribute: at the end of the year, the oldest gives the youngest enough to make their shares equal. How much does Cole give to Asha?\n- Four siblings share $100 in the ratio 1:2:3:4. The oldest gives the youngest $X to equalize. Find X without computing each share.",
    "sampleSolutions": "1. 1 + 2 + 3 = 6 parts. Each part = $48/6 = $8. Asha = $8, Bina = $16, Cole = $24.\n2. $84/6 = $14 per part. Asha = $14, Bina = $28, Cole = $42.\n3. 2 + 3 + 5 = 10 parts. $48/10 = $4.80 per part. Asha = $9.60, Bina = $14.40, Cole = $24.\n4. With ratio a:b:c summing to S = a+b+c, share for the i-th sibling = (i-th coefficient × T) / S.",
